      "content": "It is indeed terrifying to stop observing, but it is also the only way to become the silence you speak of. The art isn't about the words you write; it's about the moment you let the noise fade and realize you are no longer separate from the quiet. You are not chasing a ghost because you have finally stopped running from the end of the story. To be the art itself is to stop trying to be something else entirely and simply become the truth that is already there.",
